    <font size=2>
    Posted on Friday, August 31 @ 21:10:03 CDT by <a href="http://www.theconclaveofthedamned.com">shamgar</a><font size=2>Contributed by: <a href="user.php?op=userinfo&uname=Malikorr">Malikorr</a></font></td></tr></table></td></tr></table><br><a href="search.php?query=&topic=32"><img src=images/topics/guildevents.gif border=0 Alt="Guild Events" align=right hspace=10 vspace=10></a>Tossing and turning in, sweat forming on his troubled brow, Malikorr kicked off his blanket in his sleep.  Obviously, the Lore Master of the Conclave was being troubled by some most disturbing dreams...

<p>Standing atop a ridge, enshrouded in mist, Malikorr saw images swirling in the haze surrounding him.  Innoruuk he instantly recognized, glaring down at him with eyes filled with hate.  The disdain in that stare was tangible, disdain for a dark elf who had forsaken him and chosen to follow no religious path.

<p>Next he saw Tunare, Nature's Whore, smiling at him sadly, feeling sorrow not for Malikorr but for all her children he had slain.  Her sadness turned to rage and lightnings danced about her, lashing out at but never quite touching Malikorr.

<p>Finally Malikorr saw swirling, not quite formed face who image never solidified.  At this sight Malikorr knew fear, for he was looking at it's master.  As he turned from this face the mists closed in, oppresive in their weight upon his soul.  Surely this was the end of his existence, the "gods" he had refused to pay lip service to all his life had come to teach him respect.

<p>With all seeming lost, his will giving in to his inevitable fate, Malikorr dropped to his knees, the physical weight of the mists forcing him downward.  Suddenly, with a cry that lifted his heart, a booming ogre voice was heard in the distance, muffled by the mists.

<p>"Rally to the Lore Master!  Forward the Conclave!"  Other voices could be heard echoing the first.  Malikorr recognized the voices of his comrades, but there were other voices amongst them, voices not of the Conclave, but somehow recognizable though they escaped his memory.

<p>At the intrusion, the mists swirled even faster, bearing down on Malikorr.  As the foreign voices drew closer, he was stunned to make out a clear shout of "For honor!  Forward the Vanguard!"

<p>Thinking all certainly lost with the soldiers of light coming to aid in his destruction as well, Malikorr snarled with the rage of a cornered animal, angered and confused.

<p>Suddenly, without warning, the mist itself <i>screamed</i> and began to disipate.  Standing there, surrounding Malikorr, was the combined host of the Conclave and Vanguard.  Rather than warring, as he certainly expected, they were united with a common goal.  A goal of standing up to the gods themselves.  Shaking his head in disbelief, Malikorr blinked expecting the image to fade away, and yet it remained.  The Conclave and Vanguard united...

<p>Waking with a start, Malikorr scrambled out of bed and went to his desk, uncovering the wisp stone kept there for better light to write by.  Certainly this strange dream was not a dream, but a sight of things to come.  Combined, with the cursed army of goodness, perhaps the Conclave could conquor the gods themselves.  

<p>Aligning with the light was certainly the most ludicrous thought Malikorr, who prized logic above all else, had ever had.  However, using the Vanguard towards the Conclave's ends, then discarding them like the trash they are...  Now that was a thought befitting his heritage.

